Sampling profiler: PS2X_PROFILE=2 also says who called the system code a sample lands in. For a sample outside the executable (the heap, memcpy, locks, waits) the stack is unwound with the x64 unwind data while the thread is still suspended, up to the first return address inside the executable, and every 15 seconds the hottest (leaf, caller) pairs per thread are printed after the usual report ([profile:callers]). PS2X_PROFILE=1 is unchanged. In Metropolismania's city the game thread's heap time shows up as operator new, its memmove/memchr as byte vectors growing, and its waits as the GS queue drain; the run is as fast as with PS2X_PROFILE=1 (37.0 against 37.2 fps).

